Problem 10
✏️ Steps / Flow
Assume the first element is unique.
Compare each element with the previous unique element.
If it is different, move it to the next unique position.
Continue until the end of the list.
Return the total number of unique elements.

START

Input sorted list nums

index = 0

FOR i = 1 TO length(nums) - 1
    IF nums[i] ≠ nums[index] THEN
        index = index + 1
        nums[index] = nums[i]
    END IF
END FOR

Return index + 1

STOP
